            <ArticleTitle>[Effects of morphine and naloxone on pain sensitivity after radiation injuries in rats].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>453-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Radiation in doses 150 Gy induces different changes in pain sensitivity in rats by thermal (analgesia) and electrical (hyperalgesia) stimuli. Naloxone (0.1 and 1 mg/kg) and morphine (5 mg/kg) show, that analgesia is realized due to opioid mechanisms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
